/*
 * EXAMPLE 1 — Stack<String>, singular case.
 *
 * The test string is the sequence of blocks; the inputs block pins down every
 * CLIENT_INPUT so the sequence can be run once, concretely, with each
 * precondition checked before its call and each postcondition after it.
 *
 * The two pushes get different elements so the run distinguishes "pop returned
 * the top" from "pop returned something".  Neither pop nor peek appears in the
 * inputs block: they take no parameters, and what they return is SERVER_OUTPUT.
 */
test StackDryRun {
    sequence: push -> push -> pop -> peek;

    inputs {
        push[0].elem = "alpha";
        push[1].elem = "beta";
    }
}
